  "core_design_rules": [
    "Monk has two distinct combat paths: Pressure Arts for fragile backline targets and Combo Arts for durable enemies.",
    "The combo engine should not be the default answer to every target type.",
    "Martial Flow provides randomness as bonus momentum, not as permission for the turn to matter.",
    "Triple Attack is implemented as a Follow-Up Strike engine rather than full martial Extra Attack progression.",
    "Spirit Spheres are the main burst resource and connect pressure, combo, and finisher play.",
    "Asura Strike is the ultimate Spirit conversion tool and should remain expensive, committal, and decisive."
  ]
}